  "964440": {
    "id": "mc-hell-is-others",
    "source": "metacritic",
    "score": 78,
    "tier": "Strong",
    "numReviews": 4,
    "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/game/hell-is-others/critic-reviews/",
    "summary": "Adam Smithson does his best to exist in his tiny apartment, alone, high above Century City. His only companion is a bonsai tree, which he dutifully cares for - perhaps only to pass the time. Time which seems to have no beginning or end. But like everything else in the city, his plants require blood to survive. So Adam is forced to find a regular supply on the dark streets below. \n\nA unique, multiplayer online extraction game, Hell is Others allows you to progress your character by way of customizable items you obtain for your apartment. Grow your own ammunition via blood-thirsty plants, explore the noir urban setting, confront The Others, and do your best to live to see another day... A day which never seems to come.",
    "isVerified": true,
    "isSynthetic": false
  },
  "968870": {
    "id": "mc-close-to-the-sun",
    "source": "metacritic",
    "score": 66,
    "tier": "Fair",
    "numReviews": 38,
    "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/game/close-to-the-sun/critic-reviews/",
    "summary": "It’s 1897. Deep in international waters, the Helios stands still. Dark clouds loom overhead as unforgiving waves crash against the hull. Colossal effigies of gold, decorated with magnificent finery, stretch as far as the eye can see.\r\n\r\nBorn of Nikola Tesla’s vision, the Helios serves as a haven for the greatest scientific minds. An unbound utopia for research, independent from state and isolated from the gaze of society. Free to push the boundaries of matter and time.\r\n\r\nJournalist Rose Archer steps aboard the Helios in search of her sister Ada. She quickly discovers not all is as it seems. Grand halls stand empty. The stench of rotting flesh lingers in the air. Silence. A single word is painted across the entrance… QUARANTINE!",
    "isVerified": true,
    "isSynthetic": false
  },
  "972660": {
    "id": "mc-spiritfarer",
    "source": "metacritic",
    "score": 84,
    "tier": "Mighty",
    "numReviews": 37,
    "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/game/spiritfarer/critic-reviews/",
    "summary": "A cozy management game about dying. \r\n\r\nWhat will you leave behind?\r\nPlay as Stella, ferrymaster to the deceased, a Spiritfarer. Build a boat to explore the world, then befriend and care for spirits before finally releasing them into the afterlife. \r\n\r\nA unique, endlessly varied adventure!\r\nFarm, mine, fish, harvest, cook, and craft your way across mystical seas. Unwind for hours into cozy and relaxing gameplay. Join the adventure as Daffodil the cat, in two-player cooperative play.\r\n\r\nLearn how to say goodbye.\r\nExperience moving, emotional stories filled with unforgettable moments. Spend relaxing quality time with your spirit passengers, create lasting memories, and, ultimately, learn how to say goodbye to your cherished friends. What will you leave behind?",
    "isVerified": true,
    "isSynthetic": false
  },
