  "1266030": {
    "id": "mc-the-pale-beyond",
    "source": "metacritic",
    "score": 77,
    "tier": "Strong",
    "numReviews": 11,
    "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/game/the-pale-beyond/critic-reviews/",
    "summary": "Five years ago, The Viscount and its crew set sail through The Pale Passage in search of absolute magnetic South. The ship and its crew were tragically lost to the ice, never to be seen again. Her sister ship, The Temperance shall follow in her path, hoping to find answers where The Viscount failed.\n\nYou didn't ask to lead this expedition, but here you are. Stuck in the ice, Captain missing, miles from civilisation. Someone has to take charge.\n\nManage your meagre resources, balance safety and morale, make the hard calls, and head in the only direction you can - through The Pale Beyond.",
    "isVerified": true,
    "isSynthetic": false
  },
  "1269640": {
    "id": "mc-beacon-pines",
    "source": "metacritic",
    "score": 84,
    "tier": "Mighty",
    "numReviews": 16,
    "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/game/beacon-pines/critic-reviews/",
    "summary": "Beacon Pines is a cute and creepy adventure set within a mysterious book. You play as both the reader of the book and its main character, Luka.\r\n\r\nSomething strange is happening at the old warehouse, and Luka and his friends seem to be the only ones taking notice. Sneak out late, make new friends, uncover hidden truths, and collect words that will change the course of fate!\r\n\r\nAs the book's reader, you'll navigate the story's turning points using The Chronicle: an interactive story tree that branches and grows along with your choices. Exploring one set of events can unlock new charms to use on another branch, leading you to jump back and forth between entirely different versions of the story in order to unravel the mysteries at the heart of Beacon Pines.",
    "isVerified": true,
    "isSynthetic": false
  },
